2026-09-16 | Task: ES256 JWT verification via Supabase JWKS | Status: ready for commit/push | Summary: Replaced HS256 hono/jwt verification with ES256 verification against the Supabase Auth JWKS (jose, edge-cached 10min/30s cooldown) because the linked project signs tokens with asymmetric keys and the stored SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET was a placeholder. Added auth.ts middleware, test-auth.ts ES256 helper with a local mock JWKS HTTP server, auth.test.ts (valid token, missing token, rogue key, expired token, per-origin cache), and migrated index.test.ts to minted ES256 tokens. Live E2E passed (scripts/e2e-sos-live.mjs): admin-created temp user, real password-grant token, POST /sos 201, idempotent 200, garbage-token 401, full artifact cleanup. Quality gates passed: tests (36), typecheck, lint, security review (no secrets logged, verification edge-local), performance review (single cached JWKS fetch, no per-request DB round trip). Commit message: fix(auth): verify Supabase JWT signatures via project JWKS
2026-09-16 | Task: PATCH /sos/:id/resolve (PRD §7 #11) | Status: ready for commit/push | Summary: Implemented authenticated PATCH /sos/:id/resolve for PIC/SUPER_ADMIN. Authorization reads the application role from public.users via service-role REST (JWT payload only carries the Supabase role), rejecting WARGA with 403. Idempotent race-safe semantics via conditional PostgREST PATCH (id=eq.X & status=eq.PENDING, return=representation): success 200, same-resolver retry 200 alreadyResolved=true, other responder 409, missing event 404, malformed id 400, db failure 502. SosEvent type extended with resolved_by/resolved_at. Tests: 9 new resolve cases (46 total incl. FCM/auth), all gates pass (46 tests, typecheck, lint, security review, performance review). Live E2E extended in scripts/e2e-sos-live.mjs: Warga 403, promoted-PIC 404 on missing, 200 with resolved_by, idempotent retry, garbage token 401; full artifact cleanup. Commit message: feat(sos): add resolve endpoint for PIC responders
